{
  "requirement": "Agents SHOULD NOT anchor a file under {cite}`requirements.references.anchors` when a more precise reference is available, such as a reference attached to the Rust item that implements or tests the definition. Habeas's bundled agent skills MUST give this direction.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** The subject `requirements.references.anchors.guidance` has two parts.\n- The first is a behavioral SHOULD NOT for agents: don't anchor a file when a more precise reference is available. Tests can't check agent behavior directly.\n- The second is a testable MUST: Habeas's bundled agent skills must give this direction.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_limit_anchors_to_files_whose_items_cannot_carry_references]` is marked `{test}`.\n- It takes the bundled `habeas` skill file `references/syntax-details.md`. The helper `skill_file` reads it through `include_str!` from `assets/skills/habeas/references/syntax-details.md`, so it is the shipped asset.\n- It extracts the `## Anchors` section with `section`.\n- It asserts with `assert_text` that the section contains two phrases:\n  - \"When a file that implements or tests a requirement cannot carry a reference\", which is the condition under which anchoring is appropriate.\n  - \"Don't anchor a file whose items can carry a reference themselves\", which is the direction not to anchor when a more precise reference is available.\n- `assert_text` panics if a phrase is missing, so both assertions are enforced. The helpers are reached from the marked test and need no marks of their own.\n\n**Other skills.** A text search of `assets/skills` for \"anchor\" found anchor guidance only in `assets/skills/habeas/references/syntax-details.md#section[Anchors]`. The other skills, such as `habeas-refactor`, mention anchors only to say that `habeas refactor` rewrites them. They give no guidance on when to anchor, so no other skill needs a test for this obligation.\n\n**Result.** The test covers the one testable MUST with a relevant assertion on the shipped text. I found no gap.",
  "references": "77be7baf354b792765d3ad558009f6e3739d9b6a280baba1ff5c190c2977ee0d",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.references.anchors.guidance",
